<title>SOUTH KOREA: Dainong official denies takeover talk.</title>
<headline>Dainong official denies takeover talk.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Dainong Corp official on Thursday denied speculation that the company, South Korea's largest cotton textile maker, and its affiliate, Midopa Department Store Co Ltd, were targets of takeover bids.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe there is no danger of an M&amp;A attempt on either companies, and the rise in share price is really due to speculative buying,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>In late morning trading on Thursday, Dainong shares were up 570 won to their upper limit of 7,740. Midopa shares rose 2,200 won to their limit of 30,700.</p>
<p>Both Dainong and Midopa are units of the Dainong Group.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5649</p>
</text>
